{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZtPQVuoLuSqe6K271cz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field with enum `OrderStatus { ACTIVE, CANCELLED }`. Modify the data class to include the status.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order. Actually, since OrderRepository doesn't know about Shipment, I'll add `findAllShipmentsByOrderId()` to ShipmentRepository instead.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findAllByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, return it with 200 (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment for this order is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (all-or-nothing)\n   - Otherwise, set order status to CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments, save, and return 200\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — In the `create()` method, check if the order exists and is not CANCELLED. If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with new error code.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** — Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code to the ErrorCode enum.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests for:\n   - Cancel an active order (should succeed, return order with CANCELLED status)\n   - Cancel an already cancelled order (should succeed, return order with CANCELLED status)\n   - Cancel when a shipment is CONFIRMED (should return 409, nothing changes)\n   - Cancel a non-existent order (should return 404)\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add tests for:\n   - Creating a shipment for a cancelled order (should return 409)\n   - Creating a shipment for a non-existent order (should still work as before - only check existence in order tests)\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:** I could use a different status field name (e.g., `cancelled: Boolean`), but using an explicit enum is more extensible and clearer for future statuses.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Cancel active order**: POST → OrderController.cancel() → check order exists (404 if not) → check no CONFIRMED shipments (409 if any) → set status to CANCELLED → find all CREATED shipments and set their status to CANCELLED → save order and shipments → return 200 with order\n- **Cancel already cancelled order**: Same flow, but status is already CANCELLED so no change to shipments → return 200 with order (idempotent)\n- **Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment**: check order exists (404 if not) → check shipments (409 if CONFIRMED found) → throw ConflictException, nothing changes\n- **Create shipment for cancelled order**: POST → ShipmentController.create() → check order exists (don't fail if not) → check order is not CANCELLED (409 if CANCELLED) → create shipment\n- **Create shipment for non-existent order**: Same as before - no check needed based on requirement\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- New order creation should set status to ACTIVE (test update existing test or add new one)\n- Cancel active order returns 200, order has CANCELLED status, and CREATED shipments are cancelled\n- Cancel already-cancelled order returns 200 without changing anything\n- Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n- Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n- Creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409\n- Retrying cancel (idempotency) works correctly\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Let me start with updating the Order model:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1901,"cache_read_input_tokens":19699,"cache_creation":{"ep