ancellation state.\n\n2. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findAllByOrderId()` method to query shipments by order. This is necessary to find all shipments for an order during cancellation.\n\n3. **ApiError.kt** — Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code to enum. This is necessary for the new cancellation-related error cases.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Added `cancel()` endpoint that handles order cancellation with proper validation and shipment management. Injected ShipmentRepository. This is the core implementation.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added check to prevent creating shipments for cancelled orders. Injected OrderRepository. This is necessary to enforce the cancellation constraint.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Updated existing tests to expect status field, added 6 new tests for cancel behavior. This verifies all acceptance criteria.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Updated reset to clear orderRepository, parameterized createShipment to accept orderId, added 1 new test for cancelled order rejection. This verifies shipment constraint.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All criteria are satisfied.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint to allow customers to cancel orders before carrier confirmation, with proper status tracking and idempotent retries.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt — Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order model\n- ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findAllByOrderId() method to support order cancellation workflow\n- ApiError.kt — Added ORDER_CANCELLED error code for new error cases\n- OrderController.kt — Added cancel endpoint with all-or-nothing transactional semantics and shipment cancellation\n- ShipmentController.kt — Added validation to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders\n- OrderControllerTest.kt — Updated to test status field and added 6 tests for cancel behavior\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Updated reset method and added test for cancelled order constraint\n\nTests: